# Delta hedging

The experiment of replicating an option with the underlying: [`delta_hedge`](hedging/delta_hedge.md) rebalances a Black-Scholes delta along a given spot path and reports the portfolio, the cash account and the hedging error against the option value, which is the error of discrete rebalancing (it vanishes as the rebalancing becomes continuous, and it is not zero when the path was not generated by the model hedged with).

## The Surface

| Symbol | What it is |
|---|---|
| [`DeltaHedgeResult`](hedging/DeltaHedgeResult.md) | The option value, the hedge, the cash and the hedging error along a path. |
| [`delta_hedge`](hedging/delta_hedge.md) | Delta-hedges the field's European option along a spot path, with the delta of the field's own model and engine, and reports the hedging error. |

